    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHY THIS FACT IS `open` AND ITS 8-BIT SIBLING IS `proved`. F:fp8-add-monotone-rne is settled by enumerating all 2^24 fp8 E5M2 triples in about three seconds. The identical proposition at binary16 is 2^48 triples, so brute force is gone, and the symbolic route is where axeyum currently cannot follow: the fp8 version of this query -- three free symbols and four fp.add circuits -- ran 50 minutes in a release build without deciding, and binary16 is strictly larger. bitwuzla settles the binary16 file in 8.3 seconds.\n\nSO THIS IS A MEASURED PARITY GAP, WRITTEN DOWN AS A TARGET. `epistemic_status` is a statement about THIS ledger, and the honest value is `open`: we have not established it. `external_status` is `proved` because two independent solvers have. The evidence array is empty on purpose -- a filled one would read as axeyum having done the work.\n\nWHAT WOULD CLOSE IT. Nothing about the mathematics; the statement follows from monotonicity of correct rounding. The gap is entirely in the FP-to-bit-vector route's throughput on a multi-operand comparison miter. `artifacts/facts/smt2/neg-fp16-add-monotone-rne.smt2` is the reproducible target, byte-identical to the file the two oracles were timed on.\n\nARITY IS THE WALL, NOT WIDTH. F:fp32-doubling-add-equals-mul-two is a UNARY claim at binary32 and was enumerated over all 2^32 inputs in 51 seconds. Ternary claims lose brute force at 8 bits already. That is why this fact and its 8-bit sibling exist as a pair.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
